   "name": "Fundamentals of database management systems",
   "credits": 4,
   "offered_to": "UG",
   "description": "This is a first course on database systems at the undergraduate level, covering fundamentals concepts, aspects of database design, database query languages and database system implementation. Students are taught concepts and algorithms in a general setting that is not tied to any one particular database system. The course emphasizes both theory and application of database systems. The course includes hands-on experience of designing and using databases, and building small\ndatabase-backed applications.",
